cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Oracle-Referenced, Audited Benchmark for Stealthy False-Data Injection in
  Power-System State Estimation and Load-Frequency Control (pilot)
message: Simulation pilot; please cite the repository and state that results are synthetic.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Project authors
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-19'
keywords:
  - false data injection
  - state estimation
  - load frequency control
  - Neyman-Pearson oracle
  - benchmark audit
abstract: >-
  A notebook that builds a randomized power-grid benchmark from scratch, measures every
  detector against a hardness-indexed Neyman-Pearson oracle, audits the benchmark for
  shortcuts (including the SCEPTRE dataset), and converts detection into frequency damage.
